-- int-tests-decisions: IP27, the decisions of the Commissioner that other provisions name. Groups G3, G4, G5, G6 and G8 PRODUCE a `Decision of the Commissioner` (a subject and an outcome); group G8 (Article 33: who may appeal what)
-- and group G9 (Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3): which decisions the Commissioner's staff may not take) CONSUME them. A producer that picks the wrong outcome constructor silently turns an appealable decision into "no appeal is given by Part 8"
-- (G8's FRAGMENT, nouns request 9), so each producer's output is run through the consumers here.  EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from the Law before this module was run:
--   Article 33(1)(a), (b): an applicant for registration may appeal a decision to refuse to register it, or to refuse to register it in the restricted section; 33(2)(a) to (e): a registered charity may appeal a decision to deregister it,
--   to refuse permission to change its name or add a name (Article 12(4)), to require it to apply to change its name (12(6)), to refuse approval of an amendment of its purposes (13(3)) or of its public benefit statement (13(4)(b));
--   33(3): a person served with a notice under Article 26 or a required steps notice, the requirement; 33(4): the Attorney General, any decision. No other decision is listed (the list is closed on the reading taken).
--   Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3): the Commissioner's staff may not take (a) the decision under Article 11 on whether to register a charity, (b) the decision under Article 15(3) on whether to refuse to deregister a charity,
--   (c) the decision under Article 16 on whether to deregister a charity.

§ `Integration layer -- IP27: the decisions of the Commissioner`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

GIVEN d IS A MAYBE `Decision of the Commissioner` @desc The decision, if the producing group produced one
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision that was produced` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
      WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "the producing group produced no decision"
      WHEN JUST decision THEN decision

GIVETH AN `Appellant under Article 33`
`an applicant for registration` MEANS
    `Appellant under Article 33` WITH `an applicant for registration` IS TRUE, `a registered charity` IS FALSE, `the Attorney General` IS FALSE, `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS FALSE, `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS FALSE
GIVETH AN `Appellant under Article 33`
`a registered charity` MEANS
    `Appellant under Article 33` WITH `an applicant for registration` IS FALSE, `a registered charity` IS TRUE, `the Attorney General` IS FALSE, `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS FALSE, `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS FALSE
GIVETH AN `Appellant under Article 33`
`the Attorney General` MEANS
    `Appellant under Article 33` WITH `an applicant for registration` IS FALSE, `a registered charity` IS FALSE, `the Attorney General` IS TRUE, `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS FALSE, `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS FALSE
GIVETH AN `Appellant under Article 33`
`a person served with a notice` MEANS
    `Appellant under Article 33` WITH `an applicant for registration` IS FALSE, `a registered charity` IS FALSE, `the Attorney General` IS FALSE, `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS TRUE, `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS FALSE

GIVEN who IS AN `Appellant under Article 33` @desc The appellant
      decision IS A `Decision of the Commissioner` @desc The decision appealed
GIVETH A `Right of appeal under Article 33`
`the right of` who `to appeal` decision MEANS
    `Art 33 the right of appeal` ((fleet)'s `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) (`Appeal under Article 33` WITH appellant IS who, `decision appealed` IS decision, `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration` IS TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `Each producer's decision into Article 33 (group G8)`

-- Group G4, Article 11: an applicant refused registration (the political-party applicant of headline (a)'s scenarios) has the right of 33(1)(a).
GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application of a company with a political party purpose` MEANS
    `Int fx the application with body replaced` (`Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `Int fx the registered school company`
        `charity test facts` IS `Int fx the charity test facts with` `Int fx a determination that public benefit is provided`
        application IS `Int fx a complete application lodged on` (YMD 2026 6 1)
        findings IS `Int fx clear findings`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS `Int fx a registered office in Jersey at` "1 Esplanade, St Helier"
        `opinion on the name` IS `Int fx a name with no objection` "Gorey Schools Limited"
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY)
        (`Body in the case` WITH
            name IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
            standing IS `an applicant for registration`
            purposes IS LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` `Int fx a political party purpose`)
            facts IS (`Int fx the registered school company`)'s facts
            model IS `Int fx clear model facts`
            people IS (`Int fx the registered school company`)'s people)
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision refusing registration` MEANS `the decision that was produced` ((`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of a company with a political party purpose`)'s decision)
#ASSERT `the right of` `an applicant for registration` `to appeal` `the decision refusing registration` EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(a)`
-- Group G3, Article 9(6): an applicant refused entry in the restricted section has the right of 33(1)(b).
#ASSERT `the right of` `an applicant for registration` `to appeal` (`Art 9(6) the decision of the Commissioner on the request for the restricted section` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(b)`
-- Group G4, Article 12(4): a charity refused permission to change its name (the new name is undesirable): 33(2)(b). Article 12(6): required to apply to change its name: 33(2)(c).
#ASSERT `the right of` `a registered charity` `to appeal` (`the decision that was produced` (`Art 12(4) what the Commissioner must do on the application for permission` TRUE)) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(b)`
#ASSERT `the right of` `a registered charity` `to appeal` (`the decision that was produced` (`Art 12(6) the decision of the Commissioner on whether to require the charity to apply` TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(c)`
-- Group G5, Article 13: refusing approval of an amendment of purposes (13(3)): 33(2)(d); of the public benefit statement (13(4)(b)): 33(2)(e); refusing the prior permission of 13(5)(b): none is listed.
#ASSERT `the right of` `a registered charity` `to appeal` (`Art 13 the decision of the Commissioner` `approval of a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)(b)` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(d)`
#ASSERT `the right of` `a registered charity` `to appeal` (`Art 13 the decision of the Commissioner` `approval of a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(e)`
#ASSERT `the right of` `a registered charity` `to appeal` (`Art 13 the decision of the Commissioner` `prior permission to remain entered in the restricted section on the basis of a different condition, Article 13(5)(b)` FALSE) EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- Group G6: deregistering the charity (Article 16): 33(2)(a); deregistering on its own application (15(3), F8.16 reading taken): 33(2)(a); refusing to deregister it (15(3)(b)): not listed.
#ASSERT `the right of` `a registered charity` `to appeal` (`Art 16 the decision of the Commissioner` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(a)`
#ASSERT `the right of` `a registered charity` `to appeal` (`Art 15(3) the decision of the Commissioner` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(a)`
#ASSERT `the right of` `a registered charity` `to appeal` (`Art 15(3) the decision of the Commissioner` FALSE) EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
-- Group G8: the decision to impose a requirement in a notice under Article 26 or a required steps notice: the person served may appeal (33(3)).
#ASSERT `the right of` `a person served with a notice` `to appeal` (`Art 26 the decision of the Commissioner to impose a requirement` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(3)`
#ASSERT `the right of` `a person served with a notice` `to appeal` (`Art 27 the decision of the Commissioner to impose a requirement` TRUE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(3)`
-- The Attorney General may appeal any decision of the Commissioner (33(4)), whichever group produced it.
#ASSERT `the right of` `the Attorney General` `to appeal` (`Art 13 the decision of the Commissioner` `prior permission to remain entered in the restricted section on the basis of a different condition, Article 13(5)(b)` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`
#ASSERT `the right of` `the Attorney General` `to appeal` (`Art 15(3) the decision of the Commissioner` FALSE) EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`

§§ `Each producer's decision into Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) (group G9): which decisions the Commissioner's staff may not take`

GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
g9 MEANS `Int the reading of Schedules 1 and 2` `calendar months`
-- Reserved: the decision under Article 11 (both outcomes), under Article 15(3) (both, on the reading taken of F9.8), and under Article 16.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` g9 `the decision refusing registration`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` g9 (`Art 15(3) the decision of the Commissioner` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` g9 (`Art 15(3) the decision of the Commissioner` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` g9 (`Art 16 the decision of the Commissioner` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` g9 (`Art 16 the decision of the Commissioner` FALSE)
-- Not reserved: the restricted section (F9.16, reading taken), the name (Article 12), the approvals of Article 13 and the requirements of Articles 26 and 27.
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` g9 (`Art 9(6) the decision of the Commissioner on the request for the restricted section` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` g9 (`the decision that was produced` (`Art 12(4) what the Commissioner must do on the application for permission` TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` g9 (`Art 13 the decision of the Commissioner` `approval of a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)(b)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` g9 (`Art 26 the decision of the Commissioner to impose a requirement` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` g9 (`Art 27 the decision of the Commissioner to impose a requirement` TRUE)
